The PR is, at best, a meta-tactical[*] decision to see whether you
can "quickly" get a character past a certain AC niveau, or die to
quickly start another one without loss of real time. If you don't
mind killing your characters until you get one that "accidentally"
survives[**], it's okay.

Janis

[*] "meta"; i.e. not an in-game tactical decision, rather a player
tactical decision.

[**] "accidentally"; you need lucky games. And you have explicitly
expressed that in your original posting, where you said:
   "She was hoping for a bag of holding, magic lamp, or perhaps
   just some better armor or weapons."
The key observation is that you have to *hope* for an advantageous
good sequence of RNG events.


